Desert Dungeon rooms in Realmforge

Source:    Desert Dungeon 1.0.1, an addon for DungeonZ, by D1scoball and Globox_Z
           https://modrinth.com/mod/desert-dungeon-dungeonz-addon (desert-dungeon-1.0.1.jar)
Copyright: D1scoball and Globox_Z, 2024
License:   MIT. Modrinth and the jar's fabric.mod.json declare it, but the jar ships no license text and
           the addon has no public repository, so LICENSE is the standard MIT text with the authors that
           fabric.mod.json names. These rooms stay under it.

The structure templates in this folder are copied from data/dungeonz/structure/ in that jar: the rooms
of its desert dungeon. Each room's YAML sidecar names its source file.

Changed by Realmforge (2026-10-14), with `rf rooms import` and the rules in
art/rooms/desert_dungeon/rules.yaml of the Realmforge repository:
- left out: the overworld entrance, the parkour piece and the pieces bigger than 32 blocks on an axis;
- jigsaws inside a room replaced by the block they leave behind, and the connectors renamed
  realmforge:door (sides) and realmforge:shaft (up, down);
- templates written back in a normalized form (blocks sorted, stored deflate).
